<title>USA: Eagle USA Airfreight Q2 sales, net shr up.</title>
<headline>Eagle USA Airfreight Q2 sales, net shr up.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				 Three months ended  Six months ended</p>
<p>					    March 31,	March 31,</p>
<p>				     1997     1996	1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues		    $ 61,489 $ 39,051  $129,075 $ 79,749</p>
<p> Cost of Transportation    34,806   21,257    72,877   44,386</p>
<p>  Total			  26,683   17,794    56,198   35,363</p>
<p>Operating Expenses</p>
<p>  Personnel Costs	    14,885    9,538    29,173   18,165</p>
<p>Other Selling, General</p>
<p>   &amp; Admin. Costs	     7,773    4,926    15,802    9,609</p>
<p> Total Operating Expenses  22,658   14,464    44,975   27,774</p>
<p> Operating Income	     4,025    3,330    11,223    7,589</p>
<p>Other Income (Expense), Net</p>
<p>					701	295	 974	327</p>
<p>Income before Income Taxes</p>
<p>				    4,726    3,625    12,197    7,916</p>
<p>Provision for Income</p>
<p>   Taxes (a)		    1,778    1,519     4,735    3,267</p>
<p>  Net Income		    2,948    2,106     7,462    4,649</p>
<p>Weighted Avg. Common</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding (b)   18,643   18,692    18,554   17,512</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share (b)	0.16     0.11	0.40     0.27</p>
<p>NOTES: (a)  Eagle USA Airfreight was an S Corporation for federal tax purposes before initial public offering on December 6, 1995. The provision for income taxes for the six months ended March 31, 1996 includes pro forma charge of $945 which represents estimated federal taxes that would have been reported had Eagle USA been a C Corporation before December 6, 1995.</p>
<p>(b) On July 8, 1996, the board authorized a two-for-one stock split, effected in the form of a stock dividend. All references to number of shares outstanding and related per share amounts restated to reflect the split, which resulted in the issuance of 8,673 new shares.</p>
<p>Full company name is Eagle USA Airfreight Inc.</p>
